{"qid":"Q712","names":["Republic of Fiji"],"title":"Republic of Fiji","endonym":{"native":"Viti","lang":"fj"},"capsule":"Fiji was ceded to Britain by paramount chief Ratu Seru Epenisa Cakobau and other chiefs in 1874 and governed as a crown colony until independence on 10 October 1970. The republic's modern form dates to the constitutions following the military coups of 1987 under Sitiveni Rabuka, which overthrew the elected government and abrogated the 1970 constitution; Fiji was formally declared a republic in October 1987 and expelled from the Commonwealth. A further coup in 2000 and another in 2006 under Frank Bainimarama prolonged instability, though constitutional democracy was restored with the 2013 constitution and elections in 2014.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Fiji's island geography and EEZ are precisely defined; the Wikidata from-date of 1973 likely reflects a specific constitutional or republican milestone within the post-independence period.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Fiji","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiji"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 1987 Fijian coups d'état","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1987_Fijian_coups_d%27%C3%A9tat"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Sitiveni Rabuka","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sitiveni_Rabuka"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 2006 Fijian coup d'état","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2006_Fijian_coup_d%27%C3%A9tat"}],"britannica":"place/Fiji-republic-Pacific-Ocean","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Fiji","rulers":[{"qid":"Q469507","name":"Kamisese Mara","start":1987,"end":1992,"image":"Kamisese Mara.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki